# Normalize line endings on commit. Shell scripts and Gradle wrappers must
# stay LF — CRLF breaks shebangs and the `gradlew` launcher.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# ...but Windows batch launchers must KEEP CRLF. `android/gradlew.bat` is
# committed CRLF; the blanket rule above would renormalise it to LF in the
# object store and break the launcher on Windows — a supported target
# (invariant #7's checksum matrix builds there). `-text` leaves the stored
# bytes exactly as they are on every platform.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Binary — never line-ending-convert, never diff as text.
#
# The game-asset formats matter here: the scripted pipeline commits cooked
# meshes (`.mesh`, GDM1), Csound/SoX-generated WAVs, the raw R8 font atlas
# and the earth landmask (`.gray`), all of which git would otherwise sniff
# and mangle. Generator scripts stay text and diffable — the binaries they
# produce do not (see CLAUDE.md, "Asset / content pipeline tooling").
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mesh binary
*.gray binary
*.glb binary
*.blend binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.dds binary
*.skel binary
*.rgba binary
*.f32 binary
*.wasm binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary

# Lockfiles are review noise — collapse them in diffs. `-diff` makes git
# treat them as binary, so a plain `git diff Cargo.lock` prints "Bin ... bytes";
# the escape hatch is `git diff --text Cargo.lock` (or `--text` on any diff that
# needs to show one). Verified against the real dependabot bump in PR #21.
Cargo.lock -diff
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties -diff

# GitHub Linguist — this is a Rust project. Keep the language stats off the
# design corpus (docs/ is the largest thing in the repo by line count) and
# off the generated shader/asset chatter.
docs/**       linguist-documentation
*.md          linguist-documentation
reviews/**    linguist-documentation
tools/earth/*.geojson linguist-generated
